{"seq":11,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/qm-pi-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T02:42:25.559Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"15b6b012004c11f4052c5dba5823d535e87fe5d0472cbf7f3d93c058ea80cd02","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, here's the list from #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal notes. I left out Pellow Home Living as you asked.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- Ticket #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length (still open per Moss's cheat sheet).\n- Ticket PD-8841: Gate 4B chassis pool holds on double-booked gates (from Bettina's Dec 2025 cutover recap).\n- Chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change is listed as the main friction point, with no ticket number.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges (from Moss's cheat sheet).\n- Tide-table import macro failure on Terminal B. Engineering provided a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher, but no ticket number is recorded.\n- Patched manifest CSV request before the 06:00 shift (Moss's Nov 2 digest, no ticket number).\n\n**Please check before the review:** Moss's Nov 2, 2025 digest lists ticket #4419 under \"Puget Sound Operations\" for a barge slip 7 schedule sync, which is DMF's territory. The cheat sheet lists #4419 under PHL. I couldn't tell which is right, so Kwame should confirm it.\n\nI left out tickets for other accounts that showed up in the same channels: PD-4827 and the Saltmarsh items, #8812 and the Gate 4B scanner (Covey & Lark / Pellow), and the Orlavene notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
